      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_6_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Tom: Welcome to my home! My family lives in an apartment on the eighth floor in Cau Giay district.\nVisitor: Wow, your living room is so bright and airy!\nTom: Thank you. My mother placed several green plant pots near the balcony. From here, we can see the park and the lake.\nVisitor: How many bedrooms are there in your flat?\nTom: There are three bedrooms: one for my parents, one for my sister, and one for me. My bedroom has a study desk next to the window.\nVisitor: Who does the cooking in your house?\nTom: My father is an excellent cook. Our kitchen has a modern cooker, a microwave, and a big silver fridge.",
      "clozeText": "My grandparents live in an airy country house in Nam Dinh. There is a large vegetable garden in (23) ________ of the house. In the living room, there is a comfortable sofa and a television (24) ________ the wall. My grandmother loves cooking delicious meals in the (25) ________. There (26) ________ three bedrooms upstairs with wooden windows. I always enjoy visiting their peaceful (27) ________ during summer holidays.",
      "readingText": "Nguyen Du Secondary School is situated in a quiet suburb of Da Nang. The school is well known for its green and peaceful learning environment.\n\nThere are over one thousand green trees planted around the school yard, providing cool shade during hot summer days. The main school building has three floors painted pale yellow, with thirty spacious classrooms. Each classroom is equipped with an interactive smart projector, ceiling fans, and comfortable wooden desks. Students also enjoy spending their break time in the botanical garden behind the gym.\n\nThe teachers at Nguyen Du are very passionate and caring. They not only teach academic subjects but also encourage students to join clubs like music, robotics, and gardening. Nguyen Du is truly a wonderful place where students grow both in knowledge and personality.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nMy grandparents live in an airy country house in Nam Dinh. There is a large vegetable garden in (23) ________ of the house. In the living room, there is a comfortable sofa and a television (24) ________ the wall. My grandmother loves cooking delicious meals in the (25) ________. There (26) ________ three bedrooms upstairs with wooden windows. I always enjoy visiting their peaceful (27) ________ during summer holidays.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nNguyen Du Secondary School is situated in a quiet suburb of Da Nang. The school is well known for its green and peaceful learning environment.\n\nThere are over one thousand green trees planted around the school yard, providing cool shade during hot summer days. The main school building has three floors painted pale yellow, with thirty spacious classrooms. Each classroom is equipped with an interactive smart projector, ceiling fans, and comfortable wooden desks. Students also enjoy spending their break time in the botanical garden behind the gym.\n\nThe teachers at Nguyen Du are very passionate and caring. They not only teach academic subjects but also encourage students to join clubs like music, robotics, and gardening. Nguyen Du is truly a wonderful place where students grow both in knowledge and personality.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): You should write about: Which room it is; Furniture and appliances in the room; Colours of the walls and decorations; What you usually do in this room and why you love it.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
