      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_6_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Lan: Hi Linh, would you like to see my newly decorated bedroom?\nLinh: I'd love to! Wow, the pink wallpaper looks wonderful!\nLan: Thanks! My brother helped me hang these fairy lights above the bed. And look at my new study desk.\nLinh: The wooden bookshelf above your desk has so many English comic books.\nLan: Yes, I read one chapter every night before sleeping. I also keep my drawing pencils in that ceramic cup.\nLinh: It feels so warm and organized.",
      "clozeText": "Our secondary school has a modern computer room on the third floor. Students (23) ________ IT lessons here twice a week. Everyone has a separate computer connected to high-speed (24) ________. Mr. Binh, our IT teacher, teaches us how to type quickly and use educational (25) ________. We must keep the room clean and not bring any (26) ________ inside. Learning computer skills is very useful and (27) ________ for our future.",
      "readingText": "In recent years, many young families in Ho Chi Minh City choose to live in modern apartments rather than traditional street-front houses.\n\nApartment buildings offer many convenient amenities right at the doorstep. Residents can enjoy swimming pools, fitness centers, supermarkets, and children's playgrounds without traveling far. Security is also a major advantage, as trained guards and surveillance cameras operate twenty-four hours a day. Most apartments have wide balconies where residents can grow small flower pots and take in panoramic city views.\n\nHowever, apartment living also requires following common community rules. Residents must respect their neighbours by keeping noise levels low at night and maintaining cleanliness in shared corridors. Overall, apartments provide a comfortable and contemporary lifestyle for urban citizens.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nOur secondary school has a modern computer room on the third floor. Students (23) ________ IT lessons here twice a week. Everyone has a separate computer connected to high-speed (24) ________. Mr. Binh, our IT teacher, teaches us how to type quickly and use educational (25) ________. We must keep the room clean and not bring any (26) ________ inside. Learning computer skills is very useful and (27) ________ for our future.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nIn recent years, many young families in Ho Chi Minh City choose to live in modern apartments rather than traditional street-front houses.\n\nApartment buildings offer many convenient amenities right at the doorstep. Residents can enjoy swimming pools, fitness centers, supermarkets, and children's playgrounds without traveling far. Security is also a major advantage, as trained guards and surveillance cameras operate twenty-four hours a day. Most apartments have wide balconies where residents can grow small flower pots and take in panoramic city views.\n\nHowever, apartment living also requires following common community rules. Residents must respect their neighbours by keeping noise levels low at night and maintaining cleanliness in shared corridors. Overall, apartments provide a comfortable and contemporary lifestyle for urban citizens.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): You should write about: Where your dream house is located (by the sea, in the mountains, in space); Types of rooms and smart devices inside; What you will do there.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
