      "audioScript": "Leader: Welcome scout members to our weekend camp in Ba Vi National Park!\nCampers: Hooray!\nLeader: We have an exciting itinerary ahead. At 9:00 AM, we will set up our canvas tents in the clearing near the pine forest.\nLeader: At 11:30, each team will prepare lunch using fresh ingredients and portable camp stoves.\nLeader: In the afternoon, we are going on a gentle nature hike to observe mountain birds and collect unique plant leaves.\nLeader: In the evening, we will gather around the campfire to sing folk songs and roast marshmallows.\nCampers: That sounds amazing, Captain!",
      "clozeText": "Mai is one of the most active girls in my class. She has long brown (23) ________ and bright, friendly eyes. Mai is very (24) ________ because she likes drawing and writing poems for the school bulletin board. Whenever someone has a problem with English homework, she is always (25) ________ to help them. At weekends, she often joins her friends to (26) ________ cycling around West Lake. Everyone in our class (27) ________ Mai.",
      "readingText": "Cua Van is the largest floating fishing village situated in the middle of Ha Long Bay. Around three hundred families live in floating houses connected by wooden planks.\n\nChildren in the village travel to their floating primary school by small wooden sampans. In the classroom, they learn reading, writing, and ocean conservation alongside standard subjects. The villagers make a living mainly from pearl farming and fishing. Tourists visiting Cua Van are captivated by the calm emerald sea and the gentle lifestyle of the fishermen.\n\nLiving on the sea requires close mutual support among neighbours. When a tropical storm approaches, villagers work together to tie their houses securely inside sheltered limestone caves. Cua Van offers an extraordinary glimpse into marine community life.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nMai is one of the most active girls in my class. She has long brown (23) ________ and bright, friendly eyes. Mai is very (24) ________ because she likes drawing and writing poems for the school bulletin board. Whenever someone has a problem with English homework, she is always (25) ________ to help them. At weekends, she often joins her friends to (26) ________ cycling around West Lake. Everyone in our class (27) ________ Mai.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nCua Van is the largest floating fishing village situated in the middle of Ha Long Bay. Around three hundred families live in floating houses connected by wooden planks.\n\nChildren in the village travel to their floating primary school by small wooden sampans. In the classroom, they learn reading, writing, and ocean conservation alongside standard subjects. The villagers make a living mainly from pearl farming and fishing. Tourists visiting Cua Van are captivated by the calm emerald sea and the gentle lifestyle of the fishermen.\n\nLiving on the sea requires close mutual support among neighbours. When a tropical storm approaches, villagers work together to tie their houses securely inside sheltered limestone caves. Cua Van offers an extraordinary glimpse into marine community life.",
