      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_6_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "An: My alarm rings at 6:00 AM every school day. I stretch, jump out of bed, and wash my face with cool water.\nAn: At 6:15, my mother serves breakfast. I usually eat a bowl of warm beef noodle soup and drink a cup of fresh soybean milk.\nAn: After breakfast, I pack my homework notebooks into my yellow backpack and put on my uniform.\nAn: At 6:45, I walk to the bus stop at the end of our lane. The yellow school bus arrives at exactly 6:50.\nAn: On the bus, I sit next to my classmate Binh, and we chat happily about our favourite comic heroes.",
      "clozeText": "Every Monday morning, all students gather in the school (23) ________ for the flag-raising ceremony. We wear our white shirts and red (24) ________ neatly. The headmaster gives a short speech about weekly study plans and school (25) ________. After that, the choir sings the national (26) ________ proudly. The ceremony helps us start a new week with positive (27) ________ and motivation.",
      "readingText": "Last Friday, our secondary school held its annual Science Fair in the grand assembly hall. Over thirty scientific models were exhibited by students from grades 6 to 9.\n\nOur class presented a model of a solar-powered irrigation system. We used miniature solar panels, recycled plastic pipes, and a small water pump to demonstrate how green energy can irrigate crops automatically. Many visitors, including teachers and parents, asked questions about how the solar circuit works. My friend Nam explained the technical details with great confidence and clarity.\n\nAt the end of the fair, the headmaster announced the winning projects. Our class received the second prize for the most creative eco-friendly model. It was an inspiring day that showed how science can solve real-world challenges.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nEvery Monday morning, all students gather in the school (23) ________ for the flag-raising ceremony. We wear our white shirts and red (24) ________ neatly. The headmaster gives a short speech about weekly study plans and school (25) ________. After that, the choir sings the national (26) ________ proudly. The ceremony helps us start a new week with positive (27) ________ and motivation.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nLast Friday, our secondary school held its annual Science Fair in the grand assembly hall. Over thirty scientific models were exhibited by students from grades 6 to 9.\n\nOur class presented a model of a solar-powered irrigation system. We used miniature solar panels, recycled plastic pipes, and a small water pump to demonstrate how green energy can irrigate crops automatically. Many visitors, including teachers and parents, asked questions about how the solar circuit works. My friend Nam explained the technical details with great confidence and clarity.\n\nAt the end of the fair, the headmaster announced the winning projects. Our class received the second prize for the most creative eco-friendly model. It was an inspiring day that showed how science can solve real-world challenges.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): You should write about: Size and colour of the bedroom; Furniture inside (bed, desk, wardrobe, bookshelf); How you keep it tidy; Why it is your special place.",
