      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_6_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Librarian: Attention all teachers and students, the annual Autumn Book Fair opens today in the central hall!\nStudent: Wow, look at all these colourful book stands!\nLibrarian: We have over five thousand books on display, ranging from science fiction and historical adventures to world atlases.\nStudent: Is there a discount for secondary students?\nLibrarian: Yes! All students receive a twenty percent discount on all English storybooks and science encyclopedias.\nStudent: Can we donate old books too?\nLibrarian: Absolutely. For every three old books you donate to rural children, you receive a free handmade bookmark.",
      "clozeText": "During my trip to Hoa Binh, I visited a traditional stilt house of the Muong people. The house is built on high wooden (23) ________ to keep away from wild animals and floodwater. The roof is made of thick palm (24) ________. In the centre of the house, there is an open (25) ________ where family members cook and sit together. Visitors must take off their (26) ________ before climbing the bamboo ladder. It was an unforgettable cultural (27) ________.",
      "readingText": "Elena is a twelve-year-old girl who loves arts and crafts. Her bedroom reflects her imaginative and vibrant personality in every single corner.\n\nThe walls are painted pastel green, decorated with dozens of watercolour paintings of animals and flowers that Elena created herself. On the wooden windowsill, she cultivates small succulent plants in hand-painted ceramic mugs. Her study desk stands beneath a soft lamp, with jars of colourful markers, brushes, and sketchbooks arranged in neat rows.\n\nEvery evening after finishing her school assignments, Elena sits on a comfortable beanbag chair to read adventure novels or draw new comic strips. Her bedroom is not merely a place to sleep; it is a peaceful creative sanctuary where ideas come to life.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nDuring my trip to Hoa Binh, I visited a traditional stilt house of the Muong people. The house is built on high wooden (23) ________ to keep away from wild animals and floodwater. The roof is made of thick palm (24) ________. In the centre of the house, there is an open (25) ________ where family members cook and sit together. Visitors must take off their (26) ________ before climbing the bamboo ladder. It was an unforgettable cultural (27) ________.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nElena is a twelve-year-old girl who loves arts and crafts. Her bedroom reflects her imaginative and vibrant personality in every single corner.\n\nThe walls are painted pastel green, decorated with dozens of watercolour paintings of animals and flowers that Elena created herself. On the wooden windowsill, she cultivates small succulent plants in hand-painted ceramic mugs. Her study desk stands beneath a soft lamp, with jars of colourful markers, brushes, and sketchbooks arranged in neat rows.\n\nEvery evening after finishing her school assignments, Elena sits on a comfortable beanbag chair to read adventure novels or draw new comic strips. Her bedroom is not merely a place to sleep; it is a peaceful creative sanctuary where ideas come to life.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): You should write about: Where you are going; Who you are going with; What activities you are planning to do; How you feel about the trip.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
