      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_6_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Minh: Living at a boarding school in An Giang was challenging at first, but now I love it.\nVisitor: What was the hardest part in the beginning?\nMinh: Doing everything independently! At home, my mother washed my clothes and cleaned my room. Here, we must wash our own uniforms and tidy our dorm beds before 7:00 AM.\nVisitor: How do you spend your evenings?\nMinh: From 7:30 to 9:30 PM, we have evening study hall in the classroom. Teachers are present to answer difficult maths and English questions.\nVisitor: What do you do during weekends?\nMinh: We play sports on the field or take part in chess tournaments. It feels like one big family.",
      "clozeText": "Nam is a tall boy with broad shoulders and strong arms. He is very (23) ________ and never misses any basketball practice at school. His coach praises him for being (24) ________ and listening carefully to instructions. Nam and his teammates are (25) ________ for the inter-school tournament next Saturday. On the court, he always shows great teamwork and (26) ________ spirit. We believe his team will (27) ________ the championship trophy.",
      "readingText": "Our school library underwent a complete renovation last summer and has become the most popular facility among students.\n\nThe library now features open bookshelves, comfortable armchairs, and a dedicated silent study zone with twenty desktop computers. Students can browse through more than ten thousand books covering literature, history, natural science, and foreign languages. In addition, the librarian, Mrs. Lan, organizes a weekly book review session where students share thoughts on their favourite stories.\n\nMany students gather here during lunch breaks to work on collaborative research projects or simply enjoy a quiet reading hour. The library has fostered a wonderful reading culture across all grades in our school.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nNam is a tall boy with broad shoulders and strong arms. He is very (23) ________ and never misses any basketball practice at school. His coach praises him for being (24) ________ and listening carefully to instructions. Nam and his teammates are (25) ________ for the inter-school tournament next Saturday. On the court, he always shows great teamwork and (26) ________ spirit. We believe his team will (27) ________ the championship trophy.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nOur school library underwent a complete renovation last summer and has become the most popular facility among students.\n\nThe library now features open bookshelves, comfortable armchairs, and a dedicated silent study zone with twenty desktop computers. Students can browse through more than ten thousand books covering literature, history, natural science, and foreign languages. In addition, the librarian, Mrs. Lan, organizes a weekly book review session where students share thoughts on their favourite stories.\n\nMany students gather here during lunch breaks to work on collaborative research projects or simply enjoy a quiet reading hour. The library has fostered a wonderful reading culture across all grades in our school.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): You should write about: What subject it is; How often you have it; Who your teacher is; Why you find this subject interesting and helpful.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
