      "audioScript": "Tour Guide: Welcome visitors to Cua Van floating fishing village in Ha Long Bay.\nTourist: How long have people been living on these floating houses?\nTour Guide: For generations! The houses float on large barrels and are anchored to limestone cliffs to protect against sea storms.\nTourist: Where do children go to school?\nTour Guide: Over there! You can see the floating classroom with yellow walls. Children row their small wooden boats to class every weekday.\nTourist: What is the main food of the villagers?\nTour Guide: Fresh seafood, especially fish and crabs that they catch directly from the bay.",
      "clozeText": "On Thursday afternoons, I participate in our school science club. Our teacher, Mr. Thang, shows us how to do safe (23) ________ with water and air pressure. We wear protective white coats and plastic (24) ________ over our eyes. Yesterday, we built a small model rocket that could (25) ________ into the air. All members were amazed to see science come to (26) ________. Being in this club makes me (27) ________ science even more.",
      "readingText": "My cousin Huy is thirteen years old and attends a sports academy in Da Nang. He is tall, lean, and possesses remarkable athletic agility.\n\nHuy's passion is badminton. He started practicing with his father at the age of seven and showed exceptional hand-eye coordination early on. Currently, he trains for three hours every afternoon under the guidance of professional coaches. Despite his rigorous training schedule, Huy never neglects his schoolwork, frequently scoring top grades in English and physics.\n\nLast month, Huy represented our city at the National Junior Badminton Championship and won a silver medal. His modesty and perseverance inspire all of his peers to pursue their passions relentlessly.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nOn Thursday afternoons, I participate in our school science club. Our teacher, Mr. Thang, shows us how to do safe (23) ________ with water and air pressure. We wear protective white coats and plastic (24) ________ over our eyes. Yesterday, we built a small model rocket that could (25) ________ into the air. All members were amazed to see science come to (26) ________. Being in this club makes me (27) ________ science even more.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nMy cousin Huy is thirteen years old and attends a sports academy in Da Nang. He is tall, lean, and possesses remarkable athletic agility.\n\nHuy's passion is badminton. He started practicing with his father at the age of seven and showed exceptional hand-eye coordination early on. Currently, he trains for three hours every afternoon under the guidance of professional coaches. Despite his rigorous training schedule, Huy never neglects his schoolwork, frequently scoring top grades in English and physics.\n\nLast month, Huy represented our city at the National Junior Badminton Championship and won a silver medal. His modesty and perseverance inspire all of his peers to pursue their passions relentlessly.",
