      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_6_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Before the new semester begins, Phong and his mother visited the central bookstore to purchase supplies. Phong picked out six lined notebooks, a durable compass set, two blue gel pens, and a wooden ruler. The bookstore was crowded with cheerful parents and students preparing for school.",
      "clozeText": "Our English club organizes an 'English Only' day every Friday. On this day, we are encouraged to speak English during (23) ________ times and group discussions. There are fun language games such as spelling bee, tongue (24) ________, and word guessing. Students who speak the most English receive small (25) ________ like colourful notebooks or pens. This weekly event gives us more (26) ________ when using English in daily communication. We feel much less (27) ________ now.",
      "readingText": "The most comforting place in my grandparents' house in the countryside is undoubtedly the traditional kitchen.\n\nUnlike modern urban kitchens equipped with electric stoves and microwaves, this kitchen features a traditional wood-burning stove built from clay. Bundles of dry rice straw and firewood are stacked neatly against the wall. Copper pots and cast-iron pans hang from sturdy bamboo hooks above the hearth.\n\nMy grandmother's slow-cooked fish in clay pots has a distinct smoky aroma that cannot be replicated by any modern cooking appliance. The kitchen is always filled with warmth, delicious scents, and fond childhood memories.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nOur English club organizes an 'English Only' day every Friday. On this day, we are encouraged to speak English during (23) ________ times and group discussions. There are fun language games such as spelling bee, tongue (24) ________, and word guessing. Students who speak the most English receive small (25) ________ like colourful notebooks or pens. This weekly event gives us more (26) ________ when using English in daily communication. We feel much less (27) ________ now.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nThe most comforting place in my grandparents' house in the countryside is undoubtedly the traditional kitchen.\n\nUnlike modern urban kitchens equipped with electric stoves and microwaves, this kitchen features a traditional wood-burning stove built from clay. Bundles of dry rice straw and firewood are stacked neatly against the wall. Copper pots and cast-iron pans hang from sturdy bamboo hooks above the hearth.\n\nMy grandmother's slow-cooked fish in clay pots has a distinct smoky aroma that cannot be replicated by any modern cooking appliance. The kitchen is always filled with warmth, delicious scents, and fond childhood memories.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): You should write about: Where the library is; Books and facilities available; The rules students must follow; How the library helps your study.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
