      "audioScript": "Today our school newspaper interviews Liam, an exchange student from Sydney. Liam shares that Vietnamese students are extremely friendly and hospitable. He loves wearing the school uniform and enjoys eating traditional banh mi for breakfast. He finds Vietnamese grammar challenging but fascinating.",
      "clozeText": "The library is considered the heart of our secondary school. It contains thousands of books on science, literature, history, and foreign (23) ________. Ms. Hanh, the librarian, is always gentle and guides students to the right (24) ________. Students must keep complete (25) ________ so that others can concentrate on their studies. We can borrow up to three books for two (26) ________ before renewing. Reading here broadens our (27) ________ enormously.",
      "readingText": "The biology garden at our secondary school serves as a wonderful outdoor living classroom for grade 6 students.\n\nDivided into four quadrants, the garden showcases various plant species, including medicinal herbs, flowering bushes, root vegetables, and climbing vines. During biology classes, students observe leaf veins under magnifying glasses, record growth rates of pea shoots, and learn the life cycle of butterflies.\n\nCaring for living plants with their own hands instills in students a deep appreciation for biodiversity and ecological balance.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nThe library is considered the heart of our secondary school. It contains thousands of books on science, literature, history, and foreign (23) ________. Ms. Hanh, the librarian, is always gentle and guides students to the right (24) ________. Students must keep complete (25) ________ so that others can concentrate on their studies. We can borrow up to three books for two (26) ________ before renewing. Reading here broadens our (27) ________ enormously.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nThe biology garden at our secondary school serves as a wonderful outdoor living classroom for grade 6 students.\n\nDivided into four quadrants, the garden showcases various plant species, including medicinal herbs, flowering bushes, root vegetables, and climbing vines. During biology classes, students observe leaf veins under magnifying glasses, record growth rates of pea shoots, and learn the life cycle of butterflies.\n\nCaring for living plants with their own hands instills in students a deep appreciation for biodiversity and ecological balance.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): You should write about: Who the classmate is; His/her creative talents (drawing, singing, writing); How he/she inspires others in class.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
