      "audioScript": "Lan: Hi Mark, what are you doing with those colourful paper squares?\nMark: Hello Lan! I am folding an origami lotus flower. Doing origami is my favourite hobby.\nLan: That looks intricate! When did you start this hobby?\nMark: I started two years ago during the summer holiday. My uncle taught me basic folding techniques.\nLan: What benefits do you get from paper folding?\nMark: It trains my patience and concentration. After hours of intense maths study, folding paper brings me a peaceful feeling of relaxation.\nLan: Can you show me how to fold a paper swan this afternoon?\nMark: Of course! Bring some square paper sheets to the library at three o'clock.",
      "clozeText": "My grandfather and I share a wonderful hobby: gardening. Every Saturday morning, we spend three hours in our backyard garden. My grandfather taught me how to prepare nutrient-rich soil, sow flower seeds, and prune withered leaves. Working with living plants helps me relax after stressful school hours. I also feel immensely proud when colourful roses and sweet strawberries bloom in spring. Gardening is not only an enjoyable pastime but also teaches me patience and deep responsibility. I really love spending time outdoors in nature.",
      "readingText": "Working in the garden with my grandfather has been the most meaningful pastime of my childhood.\n\nEvery Saturday morning, we wake up at sunrise to cultivate our flourishing backyard garden. We grow a variety of organic vegetables, including juicy tomatoes, crisp lettuce, and sweet bell peppers, alongside fragrant roses. My grandfather explains how compost made from kitchen scraps nourishes the earth without using toxic chemical fertilizers.\n\nHarvesting fresh homegrown produce gives our family nutritious ingredients for weekend meals. Gardening has taught me to appreciate the natural rhythm of seasons and the value of patient labour.",
