      "audioScript": "Sophie: Hi Phong, your balcony looks full of vibrant green plants and flowers!\nPhong: Thanks Sophie! My grandfather and I spend every weekend gardening.\nSophie: Which plants do you grow most?\nPhong: We cultivate yellow marigolds, red roses, and some fresh culinary herbs like mint and basil.\nSophie: Isn't gardening very tiring?\nPhong: It requires physical effort like watering, weeding, and fertilising soil, but seeing green shoots sprout brings immense joy.\nSophie: Nature really helps people reduce stress, doesn't it?\nPhong: Absolutely! Smelling fresh earth and fragrant blossoms after school clears my mind completely.",
      "clozeText": "Maintaining good physical health is vital for secondary school students. To keep fit, teenagers should exercise regularly and follow a balanced diet. Eating plenty of fresh green vegetables and seasonal fruits provides essential vitamins for the body. You should avoid drinking too many sugary soft drinks because they can harm your teeth and cause obesity. Moreover, getting at least eight hours of sleep each night is necessary to refresh your brain. If you sit in front of computer screens for hours, remember to take short breaks to prevent eye strain. Good health helps you study much more effectively.",
      "readingText": "Adolescence is a critical stage of physical growth that demands proper nutritional balance.\n\nNutrition experts recommend that secondary students consume diverse food groups, focusing on protein-rich lean meats, calcium-packed dairy, and whole grains. Skipping breakfast should be avoided at all costs, as a healthy morning meal provides glucose for cognitive alertness during morning classes.\n\nMoreover, teenagers should limit fast food and sugary snacks, which offer empty calories and trigger skin breakouts. Developing mindful eating habits during teenage years lays the groundwork for vibrant long-term health.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nMaintaining good physical health is vital for secondary school students. To keep fit, teenagers should exercise regularly and follow a balanced diet. Eating plenty of fresh green vegetables and seasonal fruits provides essential vitamins for the body. You should avoid drinking too many sugary soft drinks because they can harm your teeth and cause obesity. Moreover, getting at least eight hours of sleep each night is necessary to refresh your brain. If you sit in front of computer screens for hours, remember to take short breaks to prevent eye strain. Good health helps you study much more effectively.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nAdolescence is a critical stage of physical growth that demands proper nutritional balance.\n\nNutrition experts recommend that secondary students consume diverse food groups, focusing on protein-rich lean meats, calcium-packed dairy, and whole grains. Skipping breakfast should be avoided at all costs, as a healthy morning meal provides glucose for cognitive alertness during morning classes.\n\nMoreover, teenagers should limit fast food and sugary snacks, which offer empty calories and trigger skin breakouts. Developing mindful eating habits during teenage years lays the groundwork for vibrant long-term health.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Healthy eating habits (fruits, vegetables, avoiding junk food); Exercise routines; Sleep schedule; Screen time management.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
