      "audioScript": "Tom: Look Minh, I finally finished assembling this miniature Boeing 787 model!\nMinh: Wow Tom, the detailing on the wings and engines is remarkable! How long did it take you?\nTom: It took me almost three weeks of careful glueing and hand-painting.\nMinh: What materials are the kit pieces made of?\nTom: Lightweight plastic and photo-etched metal parts. You need special plastic cement, tweezers, and fine acrylic paint brushes.\nMinh: It seems you need extraordinary patience for model building.\nTom: Yes, rushing ruins the small parts. It has taught me to pay attention to precision in everything I do.",
      "clozeText": "Last Sunday, our youth volunteer club organized an environmental clean-up campaign around the town lake. Over forty students woke up early in the morning and gathered at the community center. We put on rubber gloves and used bamboo tongs to pick up plastic bottles, food wrappers, and discarded bags along the shore. We sorted the collected waste into biodegradable rubbish and recyclable materials. Local residents praised our hard work and brought us refreshing drinking water. Doing community service made us feel useful and brought us closer to each other. We promised to continue this project next month.",
      "readingText": "The shore of the municipal lake had long been littered with discarded plastic trash until our school club took action.\n\nEquipped with protective gloves, bamboo trash tongs, and heavy-duty canvas sacks, fifty student volunteers conducted a massive four-hour sanitation operation. We retrieved hundreds of plastic straws, disposable styrofoam boxes, and rusted cans trapped in shoreline reeds.\n\nWe then delivered the recyclable plastics to a local sorting plant to fund our club's tree-planting initiative. The project transformed the shoreline into a clean, inviting park where local families can walk safely.",
