      "schoolName": "TRƯỜNG THCS ĐỒNG YÊN",
      "teacherName": "Thầy Đinh Văn Thành",
      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_7_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Peter: Hi Linh, look at this clay bowl! I shaped it myself at Bat Trang pottery village last Saturday.\nLinh: It looks wonderful, Peter! The green glaze and leaf pattern are so artistic.\nPeter: Shaping wet clay on a turning potter's wheel was trickier than I anticipated.\nLinh: Did an artisan guide you through the process?\nPeter: Yes, Master Hung showed me how to keep the clay centred with wet hands and apply gentle pressure.\nLinh: How long did the bowl take to fire in the kiln?\nPeter: It was baked at twelve hundred degrees Celsius for two days before cooling down.\nLinh: You must feel very proud holding something made by your own hands!",
      "clozeText": "Before the chilly winter arrived, our school launched a charity drive called 'Warm Winter for Children'. Students across all grades brought clean winter jackets, woollen scarves, and warm blankets to the school hall. We carefully inspected each item, folded them neatly, and packed them into sturdy cardboard boxes. Last weekend, our teacher representatives travelled to a remote mountainous district in Lao Cai to distribute the gifts. Seeing the joyful smiles of the young ethnic children made all of us feel warm inside. Volunteering taught us the true value of empathy and human kindness. We hope to organize more charity projects like this in the future.",
      "readingText": "Winters in the northern highlands of Lao Cai are notoriously harsh, with temperatures frequently plunging near freezing point.\n\nMany ethnic minority schoolchildren in highland hamlets lack adequate winter clothing to stay warm on their long walks to school. In response, our student union spearheaded the 'Warmth for the Highlands' winter donation drive, amassing over eight hundred woollen coats, insulated boots, and thick blankets.\n\nOur volunteer convoy navigated treacherous mountain passes to deliver the relief supplies directly to schools. Witnessing the children bundle up warmly filled our hearts with immense gratitude and fraternal love.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nBefore the chilly winter arrived, our school launched a charity drive called 'Warm Winter for Children'. Students across all grades brought clean winter jackets, woollen scarves, and warm blankets to the school hall. We carefully inspected each item, folded them neatly, and packed them into sturdy cardboard boxes. Last weekend, our teacher representatives travelled to a remote mountainous district in Lao Cai to distribute the gifts. Seeing the joyful smiles of the young ethnic children made all of us feel warm inside. Volunteering taught us the true value of empathy and human kindness. We hope to organize more charity projects like this in the future.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nWinters in the northern highlands of Lao Cai are notoriously harsh, with temperatures frequently plunging near freezing point.\n\nMany ethnic minority schoolchildren in highland hamlets lack adequate winter clothing to stay warm on their long walks to school. In response, our student union spearheaded the 'Warmth for the Highlands' winter donation drive, amassing over eight hundred woollen coats, insulated boots, and thick blankets.\n\nOur volunteer convoy navigated treacherous mountain passes to deliver the relief supplies directly to schools. Witnessing the children bundle up warmly filled our hearts with immense gratitude and fraternal love.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): The purpose of the charity campaign; Items donated (warm clothes, books, stationery); How items were packed; Delivery results.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
