      "audioScript": "Lan: Sophie, your skin looks red on your shoulders! Did you get sunburned yesterday?\nSophie: Yes Lan, I swam at the public pool at noon without wearing any sunscreen.\nLan: Midday ultraviolet rays between ten in the morning and two in the afternoon are extremely harsh.\nSophie: My shoulders sting and feel hot whenever my shirt rubs against them.\nLan: You should apply cool aloe vera gel immediately to soothe the inflammation.\nSophie: Will aloe vera help relieve the burning sensation?\nLan: Definitely! And remember to drink plenty of water and wear a wide-brimmed hat whenever you go outdoors in sunny weather.",
      "clozeText": "Every Saturday afternoon, members of our youth volunteer team visit the suburban community center to tutor primary school pupils from poor families. Many of these children cannot afford extra private classes and struggle with basic reading and mathematics. We patiently review their textbook exercises, play educational spelling games, and tell inspirational moral stories. Over the past three months, their school grades have improved significantly. More importantly, they have become much more confident and enthusiastic about going to school. Tutoring these children has shown us that sharing knowledge is one of the greatest gifts one can offer to society. It is deeply rewarding.",
      "readingText": "Education inequality presents severe hurdles for children residing in disadvantaged rural communities.\n\nTo address this gap, our school youth league initiated the 'Little Lights' tutoring program, pairing grade 7 volunteers with struggling primary pupils. Every weekend, volunteers provide individualized academic coaching, using colorful flashcards and interactive maths games to make learning enjoyable.\n\nBeyond academic gains, the program provides younger pupils with compassionate mentors who encourage them to dream boldly. The experience reinforces the transformative power of peer-led community education.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nEvery Saturday afternoon, members of our youth volunteer team visit the suburban community center to tutor primary school pupils from poor families. Many of these children cannot afford extra private classes and struggle with basic reading and mathematics. We patiently review their textbook exercises, play educational spelling games, and tell inspirational moral stories. Over the past three months, their school grades have improved significantly. More importantly, they have become much more confident and enthusiastic about going to school. Tutoring these children has shown us that sharing knowledge is one of the greatest gifts one can offer to society. It is deeply rewarding.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nEducation inequality presents severe hurdles for children residing in disadvantaged rural communities.\n\nTo address this gap, our school youth league initiated the 'Little Lights' tutoring program, pairing grade 7 volunteers with struggling primary pupils. Every weekend, volunteers provide individualized academic coaching, using colorful flashcards and interactive maths games to make learning enjoyable.\n\nBeyond academic gains, the program provides younger pupils with compassionate mentors who encourage them to dream boldly. The experience reinforces the transformative power of peer-led community education.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Where the clean-up occurred; Types of litter collected; Sorting recyclable trash; How residents reacted to your project.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
