      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_7_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Phong: Tom, why do you look so fatigued and lethargic this afternoon?\nTom: I have had a dull headache since our physical education class.\nPhong: How much water have you drunk today?\nTom: Just a small sip of soda at lunch. I often forget to carry my water bottle.\nPhong: Dehydration is probably causing your headache! Teenagers need at least one and a half to two litres of water daily.\nTom: Does drinking sufficient water really make a big difference?\nPhong: Yes! Water circulates nutrients, cools your body temperature, and keeps your brain alert. Here, drink this bottle of fresh water.\nTom: Thanks Phong, I feel refreshed already. I will bring a reusable bottle every day from now on.",
      "clozeText": "Birdwatching is an uncommon but deeply fascinating hobby that connects people with the wild beauty of nature. Equipped with lightweight binoculars and an illustrated field guide, my father and I explore the quiet trails of Ba Vi National Park at dawn. Early morning is the best time to observe birds because they are actively singing and searching for food. We have spotted over thirty distinct species, including vibrant sunbirds, clever drongos, and rare mountain thrushes. Birdwatching demands silence, keen observation, and immense patience. This rewarding pastime has deepened my passion for wildlife conservation.",
      "readingText": "Ba Vi National Park boasts extraordinary avian biodiversity thanks to its lush subtropical rainforest ecosystem.\n\nAvid birdwatchers traverse dawn mist on elevated mountain trails, listening attentively to melodic territorial bird calls before scanning canopy branches through high-magnification spotting scopes. Rare sightings include the blue-rumped pitta, silver pheasants, and majestic crested serpent eagles gliding over valleys.\n\nDocumenting wild bird behaviors without disturbing their natural habitat instills in youth an enduring dedication to ecological preservation and forest conservation.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nBirdwatching is an uncommon but deeply fascinating hobby that connects people with the wild beauty of nature. Equipped with lightweight binoculars and an illustrated field guide, my father and I explore the quiet trails of Ba Vi National Park at dawn. Early morning is the best time to observe birds because they are actively singing and searching for food. We have spotted over thirty distinct species, including vibrant sunbirds, clever drongos, and rare mountain thrushes. Birdwatching demands silence, keen observation, and immense patience. This rewarding pastime has deepened my passion for wildlife conservation.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nBa Vi National Park boasts extraordinary avian biodiversity thanks to its lush subtropical rainforest ecosystem.\n\nAvid birdwatchers traverse dawn mist on elevated mountain trails, listening attentively to melodic territorial bird calls before scanning canopy branches through high-magnification spotting scopes. Rare sightings include the blue-rumped pitta, silver pheasants, and majestic crested serpent eagles gliding over valleys.\n\nDocumenting wild bird behaviors without disturbing their natural habitat instills in youth an enduring dedication to ecological preservation and forest conservation.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Developing social responsibility; Building empathy and teamwork skills; Gaining real-world experience; Bringing happiness to others.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
