      "audioScript": "Hoa: David, you are rubbing your eyes constantly. Are they stinging?\nDavid: Yes Hoa, my eyes feel dry, irritated, and strained after finishing my online project.\nHoa: How long have you been staring at your laptop screen without taking a break?\nDavid: For nearly three continuous hours! I wanted to finish typing my science slides.\nHoa: You should practice the 20-20-20 eye rule every day.\nDavid: What does the 20-20-20 rule mean?\nHoa: Every twenty minutes, look away from the screen at an object twenty feet away for twenty seconds.\nDavid: That sounds simple! Does blinking frequently help as well?\nHoa: Yes, blinking spreads moisture evenly over your eyes and prevents redness.",
      "clozeText": "Seasonal climate transitions often bring outbreaks of viral influenza and common colds among schoolchildren. Symptoms typically include a runny nose, mild fever, sore throat, and persistent coughing. Medical practitioners advise getting ample bed rest and drinking hot herbal tea infused with fresh ginger and honey. Taking over-the-counter paracetamol can help relieve muscular aches, but antibiotics should never be taken without a doctor's prescription. Simple hygienic measures like washing hands frequently and wearing protective face masks effectively halt viral transmission.",
      "readingText": "Seasonal temperature fluctuations in autumn and winter frequently create favorable conditions for respiratory virus transmission.\n\nInfluenza spreads rapidly in crowded classrooms through airborne droplets and contaminated desk surfaces. Health authorities stress that prevention relies primarily on universal hand hygiene, regular room ventilation, and annual flu vaccination.\n\nStudents exhibiting fever or persistent coughing should isolate at home until fully recovered to protect vulnerable peers and prevent widespread school absenteeism.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nSeasonal climate transitions often bring outbreaks of viral influenza and common colds among schoolchildren. Symptoms typically include a runny nose, mild fever, sore throat, and persistent coughing. Medical practitioners advise getting ample bed rest and drinking hot herbal tea infused with fresh ginger and honey. Taking over-the-counter paracetamol can help relieve muscular aches, but antibiotics should never be taken without a doctor's prescription. Simple hygienic measures like washing hands frequently and wearing protective face masks effectively halt viral transmission.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nSeasonal temperature fluctuations in autumn and winter frequently create favorable conditions for respiratory virus transmission.\n\nInfluenza spreads rapidly in crowded classrooms through airborne droplets and contaminated desk surfaces. Health authorities stress that prevention relies primarily on universal hand hygiene, regular room ventilation, and annual flu vaccination.\n\nStudents exhibiting fever or persistent coughing should isolate at home until fully recovered to protect vulnerable peers and prevent widespread school absenteeism.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): What the hobby is; Special tools required; Skills developed; Why you find it exciting and unique.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
