      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_7_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "An: Lan, you know a lot about health. Can you give me advice about teenage skin acne?\nLan: Sure An! During puberty, hormonal changes cause sebaceous glands to produce excess oil, leading to clogged pores.\nAn: Should I wash my face multiple times with harsh antibacterial soap?\nLan: Absolutely not! Over-washing strips away natural moisture and causes skin to produce even more oil. Use a gentle cleanser twice daily.\nAn: What about squeezing or popping pimples?\nLan: Never squeeze them with your fingers! That pushes bacteria deeper and leaves permanent scars.\nAn: Are there specific foods I should avoid?\nLan: Cut down on oily fast food, chocolate, and sugary drinks. Eat fresh green veggies and drink plenty of clean water.\nAn: Thank you Lan, I will follow your gentle skincare routine consistently.",
      "clozeText": "Last Saturday, our school cooperated with the provincial blood transfusion center to host a voluntary blood donation day. Hundreds of teachers, parents, and older youths queued up enthusiastically in the school gymnasium. Medical personnel performed health screenings before safely collecting units of blood. Each donated unit of blood can save up to three lives in emergency surgical procedures. Although secondary students are too young to donate blood, we assisted by serving warm sweet milk, handing out certificates, and cheering donors.",
      "readingText": "Voluntary blood donation constitutes a cornerstone of modern public healthcare, sustaining life in emergency trauma cases and surgeries.\n\nHospitals continuously experience acute shortages of blood reserves, particularly during holiday seasons and major epidemic outbreaks. Civic campaigns organized in schools and universities mobilize hundreds of altruistic citizens who willingly donate half a liter of blood to save unfamiliar patients.\n\nVoluntary blood drives exemplify the noble humanitarian principle of mutual aid, reinforcing the profound sanctity of human life.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nLast Saturday, our school cooperated with the provincial blood transfusion center to host a voluntary blood donation day. Hundreds of teachers, parents, and older youths queued up enthusiastically in the school gymnasium. Medical personnel performed health screenings before safely collecting units of blood. Each donated unit of blood can save up to three lives in emergency surgical procedures. Although secondary students are too young to donate blood, we assisted by serving warm sweet milk, handing out certificates, and cheering donors.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nVoluntary blood donation constitutes a cornerstone of modern public healthcare, sustaining life in emergency trauma cases and surgeries.\n\nHospitals continuously experience acute shortages of blood reserves, particularly during holiday seasons and major epidemic outbreaks. Civic campaigns organized in schools and universities mobilize hundreds of altruistic citizens who willingly donate half a liter of blood to save unfamiliar patients.\n\nVoluntary blood drives exemplify the noble humanitarian principle of mutual aid, reinforcing the profound sanctity of human life.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): How students spread the message; Number of books collected; Categories of books; How the books were transported to remote schools.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
