      "audioScript": "Sophie: Phong, did you participate in the 'Green Weekend' campaign last Saturday?\nPhong: Yes Sophie, our school youth union organized a major clean-up around the district community park.\nSophie: How many secondary students turned out to help?\nPhong: Over one hundred energetic volunteers! We formed small teams equipped with rubber gloves and biodegradable trash bags.\nSophie: What kind of waste was scattered around the park?\nPhong: Mostly single-use plastic bottles, snack wrappers, and drink straws discarded near the pond.\nSophie: Did you separate recyclable materials?\nPhong: Yes, we sorted plastic bottles and aluminium cans into green recycling bins. It felt so rewarding to see the park spotless!",
      "clozeText": "Learning to play the classical guitar has been my most rewarding creative endeavor throughout grade 7. Every evening, I practice fingering chords, picking arpeggios, and following rhythmic metronomes. Last month, four friends and I founded an acoustic music band called 'The Strummers'. We rehearse harmonious folk and pop songs in the school music room every Friday afternoon. Performing live on stage during Teachers' Day celebration boosted our stage confidence enormously. Music provides a universal language that expresses emotions beyond words.",
      "readingText": "Mastering an acoustic musical instrument requires a disciplined synthesis of physical coordination, auditory sensitivity, and emotional expression.\n\nClassical guitarists must spend months developing fingertip calluses, memorizing complex chord progressions, and mastering polyphonic fingerpicking. When playing in an ensemble, musicians learn to listen attentively to their peers, synchronizing tempos and balancing acoustic dynamics.\n\nMusic education enriches neural development, enhances emotional empathy, and provides teenagers with a lifelong vehicle for profound artistic fulfillment.",
