      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_7_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "Tom: Hoa, how is the school book donation project progressing?\nHoa: Fantastic Tom! We have already gathered more than six hundred storybooks, dictionaries, and reference handbooks.\nTom: Who will receive these donated books?\nHoa: Two newly established community libraries in rural commune schools.\nTom: Books open a whole new world of imagination and knowledge for rural children.\nHoa: Exactly. Many pupils there don't have access to bookstores or public libraries.\nTom: Did students write encouraging bookmarks to insert inside each book?\nHoa: Yes! Every book contains a heartfelt message wishing the reader joy and academic success.\nTom: That small personal gesture makes the donation truly meaningful.",
      "clozeText": "Every Sunday dawn, the 'Heartfelt Bowl' charity group gathers at our community kitchen to prepare free nutritious porridge for underprivileged hospital patients. Volunteers chop fresh carrots, mince lean pork, and simmer fragrant rice in massive stainless steel cauldrons. At 7:00 AM, we transport steaming pots to the provincial hospital and distribute over four hundred bowls to elderly patients and impoverished families. Seeing their heartfelt smiles and receiving their gratitude warms our hearts deeply.",
      "readingText": "Hospitalization often places overwhelming financial strain on impoverished families travelling from remote mountain hamlets for medical treatment.\n\nGrassroots charitable initiatives like hospital charity soup kitchens alleviate this hardship by providing hot, nourishing porridge without charge every morning. Dedicated volunteer cooks ensure rigorous food sanitation while preparing wholesome broths rich in vegetables, legumes, and protein.\n\nProviding warm food directly to patients' bedsides provides essential emotional comfort and tangible solidarity during times of vulnerability.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nEvery Sunday dawn, the 'Heartfelt Bowl' charity group gathers at our community kitchen to prepare free nutritious porridge for underprivileged hospital patients. Volunteers chop fresh carrots, mince lean pork, and simmer fragrant rice in massive stainless steel cauldrons. At 7:00 AM, we transport steaming pots to the provincial hospital and distribute over four hundred bowls to elderly patients and impoverished families. Seeing their heartfelt smiles and receiving their gratitude warms our hearts deeply.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nHospitalization often places overwhelming financial strain on impoverished families travelling from remote mountain hamlets for medical treatment.\n\nGrassroots charitable initiatives like hospital charity soup kitchens alleviate this hardship by providing hot, nourishing porridge without charge every morning. Dedicated volunteer cooks ensure rigorous food sanitation while preparing wholesome broths rich in vegetables, legumes, and protein.\n\nProviding warm food directly to patients' bedsides provides essential emotional comfort and tangible solidarity during times of vulnerability.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Which sport (badminton, swimming, basketball); Practice schedule; Health benefits experienced; Friendships formed.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
