      "audioScript": "Alex: David, were you touched by our visit to the local nursing home yesterday?\nDavid: Immensely Alex! Spending time with elderly residents was the most rewarding experience of my week.\nAlex: What activities did our volunteer team organize for them?\nDavid: Lan and Phong performed traditional folk songs on the acoustic guitar, while we served hot herbal tea and soft biscuits.\nAlex: Did you talk with any of the seniors?\nDavid: Yes, I chatted with Grandpa Tam, who is eighty-two years old. He told me captivating stories about life in our province decades ago.\nAlex: Many elderly people feel lonely, so young visitors bring great cheer and comfort.\nDavid: True. We promised to return next month to teach them how to make simple origami flowers.",
      "clozeText": "Assembling miniature scale models of historic airplanes and naval ships is an absorbing hobby requiring immense focus. The hobby involves snipping tiny plastic parts from sprues, trimming flash with hobby knives, and cementing pieces together with precision glue. Once assembled, models are carefully painted with airbrushes to replicate historic camouflage markings and battle weathering. Completing an accurate 1:72 scale model of a historical Spitfire fighter gives me immense satisfaction. This hobby develops exceptional eye-hand coordination.",
      "readingText": "Scale modeling is a sophisticated hobby blending fine craftsmanship, engineering appreciation, and rigorous historical research.\n\nModelers work with hundreds of intricate injection-molded styrene components, photo-etched brass details, and microscopic waterslide decals. Replicating authentic historic weathering requires mastering airbrush shading, dry-brushing metallic wear, and applying oil washes to simulate operational grime.\n\nThis meticulous pursuit cultivates extraordinary concentration, analytical problem-solving, and patience in secondary students.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nAssembling miniature scale models of historic airplanes and naval ships is an absorbing hobby requiring immense focus. The hobby involves snipping tiny plastic parts from sprues, trimming flash with hobby knives, and cementing pieces together with precision glue. Once assembled, models are carefully painted with airbrushes to replicate historic camouflage markings and battle weathering. Completing an accurate 1:72 scale model of a historical Spitfire fighter gives me immense satisfaction. This hobby develops exceptional eye-hand coordination.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nScale modeling is a sophisticated hobby blending fine craftsmanship, engineering appreciation, and rigorous historical research.\n\nModelers work with hundreds of intricate injection-molded styrene components, photo-etched brass details, and microscopic waterslide decals. Replicating authentic historic weathering requires mastering airbrush shading, dry-brushing metallic wear, and applying oil washes to simulate operational grime.\n\nThis meticulous pursuit cultivates extraordinary concentration, analytical problem-solving, and patience in secondary students.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Small acts of kindness (holding doors, smiling, helping neighbours); How kindness spreads in a community; Why kindness makes you happier.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
