      "audioUrl": "/web-tieng-anh/audio/listening_8_gk1.mp3",
      "audioScript": "David: \"Hi Huong! What are you working on for our English group presentation?\"\nHuong: \"Hello David! I am preparing a short talk about Navigating Peer Pressure and Social Media Forums.\"\nDavid: \"That sounds very interesting! Can you share one important detail about it?\"\nHuong: \"Sure! Adolescence is a pivotal stage where teenagers feel an intense urge to fit in with their peer groups.\"\nDavid: \"I agree completely. It helps students understand more about real-life experiences.\"\nHuong: \"Yes, and we can practice speaking English with confidence during the presentation!\"",
      "clozeText": "Adolescence is a pivotal stage where teenagers feel an intense (23) ________ to fit in with their peer groups. With the omnipresence of social media forums, peer pressure often (24) ________ through digital channels, pushing teens to conform to unrealistic beauty standards or trendy lifestyle habits. Constant comparison (25) ________ idealized online profiles can erode self-confidence and fuel feelings of inadequacy. Teenagers must realize that social media (26) ________ are curated highlights rather than authentic reality. Staying true to personal values and choosing empathetic (27) ________ provides the strongest safeguard against negative peer influences.",
      "readingText": "Adolescence is a pivotal stage where teenagers feel an intense urge to fit in with their peer groups. With the omnipresence of social media forums, peer pressure often manifests through digital channels, pushing teens to conform to unrealistic beauty standards or trendy lifestyle habits. Constant comparison with idealized online profiles can erode self-confidence and fuel feelings of inadequacy. Teenagers must realize that social media feeds are curated highlights rather than authentic reality. Staying true to personal values and choosing empathetic friends provides the strongest safeguard against negative peer influences.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nAdolescence is a pivotal stage where teenagers feel an intense (23) ________ to fit in with their peer groups. With the omnipresence of social media forums, peer pressure often (24) ________ through digital channels, pushing teens to conform to unrealistic beauty standards or trendy lifestyle habits. Constant comparison (25) ________ idealized online profiles can erode self-confidence and fuel feelings of inadequacy. Teenagers must realize that social media (26) ________ are curated highlights rather than authentic reality. Staying true to personal values and choosing empathetic (27) ________ provides the strongest safeguard against negative peer influences.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nAdolescence is a pivotal stage where teenagers feel an intense urge to fit in with their peer groups. With the omnipresence of social media forums, peer pressure often manifests through digital channels, pushing teens to conform to unrealistic beauty standards or trendy lifestyle habits. Constant comparison with idealized online profiles can erode self-confidence and fuel feelings of inadequacy. Teenagers must realize that social media feeds are curated highlights rather than authentic reality. Staying true to personal values and choosing empathetic friends provides the strongest safeguard against negative peer influences.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Examples of negative peer pressure; Why teenagers feel the urge to conform; The importance of self-confidence and personal values; Choosing supportive friends.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
