      "audioScript": "Mark: \"Hi Hoa! What are you working on for our English group presentation?\"\nHoa: \"Hello Mark! I am preparing a short talk about Documenting Local History through Oral Interviews.\"\nMark: \"That sounds very interesting! Can you share one important detail about it?\"\nHoa: \"Sure! Grade 8 history students recently embarked on a local heritage project: recording oral history interviews with village elders.\"\nMark: \"I agree completely. It helps students understand more about real-life experiences.\"\nHoa: \"Yes, and we can practice speaking English with confidence during the presentation!\"",
      "clozeText": "Grade 8 history students recently embarked on a local (23) ________ project: recording oral history interviews with village elders. Armed with portable audio recorders and (24) ________ drafted questions, students gathered firsthand recollections of wartime resilience, communal traditions, and changing village landscapes. (25) ________ shared emotional memories with pride, grateful that their stories would be preserved for future (26) ________. Transcribing and archiving these oral accounts brought dry textbook history vibrantly to life. (27) ________ storytelling bridges time and deepens cultural pride.",
      "readingText": "Grade 8 history students recently embarked on a local heritage project: recording oral history interviews with village elders. Armed with portable audio recorders and thoughtfully drafted questions, students gathered firsthand recollections of wartime resilience, communal traditions, and changing village landscapes. Elders shared emotional memories with pride, grateful that their stories would be preserved for future generations. Transcribing and archiving these oral accounts brought dry textbook history vibrantly to life. Intergenerational storytelling bridges time and deepens cultural pride.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nGrade 8 history students recently embarked on a local (23) ________ project: recording oral history interviews with village elders. Armed with portable audio recorders and (24) ________ drafted questions, students gathered firsthand recollections of wartime resilience, communal traditions, and changing village landscapes. (25) ________ shared emotional memories with pride, grateful that their stories would be preserved for future (26) ________. Transcribing and archiving these oral accounts brought dry textbook history vibrantly to life. (27) ________ storytelling bridges time and deepens cultural pride.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nGrade 8 history students recently embarked on a local heritage project: recording oral history interviews with village elders. Armed with portable audio recorders and thoughtfully drafted questions, students gathered firsthand recollections of wartime resilience, communal traditions, and changing village landscapes. Elders shared emotional memories with pride, grateful that their stories would be preserved for future generations. Transcribing and archiving these oral accounts brought dry textbook history vibrantly to life. Intergenerational storytelling bridges time and deepens cultural pride.",
