      "audioScript": "Mark: \"Hi Hoa! What are you working on for our English group presentation?\"\nHoa: \"Hello Mark! I am preparing a short talk about Van Phuc Silk: The Living Weaving Tradition.\"\nMark: \"That sounds very interesting! Can you share one important detail about it?\"\nHoa: \"Sure! Van Phuc silk village, located on the banks of the Nhue River in Ha Dong, is renowned as the cradle of authentic Vietnamese silk weaving.\"\nMark: \"I agree completely. It helps students understand more about real-life experiences.\"\nHoa: \"Yes, and we can practice speaking English with confidence during the presentation!\"",
      "clozeText": "Van Phuc silk village, located on the banks of the (23) ________ River in Ha Dong, is renowned as the cradle of authentic Vietnamese silk weaving. For over a (24) ________, Van Phuc weavers have utilized natural silkworm threads to produce delicate vân silk that feels feather-light and (25) ________ soft. The rhythmic clatter of mechanical and wooden looms echoes down ancient brick-paved alleys. Village artisans create (26) ________ cloud, flower, and dragon motifs that have adorned traditional royal garments for centuries. Visiting Van Phuc (27) ________ a captivating journey into Vietnam's living textile heritage.",
      "readingText": "Van Phuc silk village, located on the banks of the Nhue River in Ha Dong, is renowned as the cradle of authentic Vietnamese silk weaving. For over a millennium, Van Phuc weavers have utilized natural silkworm threads to produce delicate vân silk that feels feather-light and extraordinarily soft. The rhythmic clatter of mechanical and wooden looms echoes down ancient brick-paved alleys. Village artisans create intricate cloud, flower, and dragon motifs that have adorned traditional royal garments for centuries. Visiting Van Phuc offers a captivating journey into Vietnam's living textile heritage.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nVan Phuc silk village, located on the banks of the (23) ________ River in Ha Dong, is renowned as the cradle of authentic Vietnamese silk weaving. For over a (24) ________, Van Phuc weavers have utilized natural silkworm threads to produce delicate vân silk that feels feather-light and (25) ________ soft. The rhythmic clatter of mechanical and wooden looms echoes down ancient brick-paved alleys. Village artisans create (26) ________ cloud, flower, and dragon motifs that have adorned traditional royal garments for centuries. Visiting Van Phuc (27) ________ a captivating journey into Vietnam's living textile heritage.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nVan Phuc silk village, located on the banks of the Nhue River in Ha Dong, is renowned as the cradle of authentic Vietnamese silk weaving. For over a millennium, Van Phuc weavers have utilized natural silkworm threads to produce delicate vân silk that feels feather-light and extraordinarily soft. The rhythmic clatter of mechanical and wooden looms echoes down ancient brick-paved alleys. Village artisans create intricate cloud, flower, and dragon motifs that have adorned traditional royal garments for centuries. Visiting Van Phuc offers a captivating journey into Vietnam's living textile heritage.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Cultural identity and national pride; Economic livelihood for rural artisans; Experiential tourism potential; How younger generations can support craft villages.",
