      "audioScript": "Alex: \"Hi Minh! What are you working on for our English group presentation?\"\nMinh: \"Hello Alex! I am preparing a short talk about Dong Ho Folk Painting: Preserving Woodblock Art.\"\nAlex: \"That sounds very interesting! Can you share one important detail about it?\"\nMinh: \"Sure! Dong Ho folk woodblock paintings, originating in Bac Ninh province, are vibrant artistic expressions of traditional Vietnamese rural life.\"\nAlex: \"I agree completely. It helps students understand more about real-life experiences.\"\nMinh: \"Yes, and we can practice speaking English with confidence during the presentation!\"",
      "clozeText": "Dong Ho folk woodblock paintings, originating in Bac Ninh (23) ________, are vibrant artistic expressions of traditional Vietnamese rural life. Artisans carve reverse designs onto dense (24) ________ wood blocks, using separate blocks for each distinct colour. Pigments are derived entirely from natural sources: (25) ________ from crushed scallop shells (điệp), black from charred bamboo leaves, red from terra cotta clay, (26) ________ yellow from gardenia seeds. Paintings depicting plump pigs, triumphant roosters, and cheerful folk (27) ________ convey heartfelt wishes for prosperity and domestic harmony.",
      "readingText": "Dong Ho folk woodblock paintings, originating in Bac Ninh province, are vibrant artistic expressions of traditional Vietnamese rural life. Artisans carve reverse designs onto dense persimmon wood blocks, using separate blocks for each distinct colour. Pigments are derived entirely from natural sources: white from crushed scallop shells (điệp), black from charred bamboo leaves, red from terra cotta clay, and yellow from gardenia seeds. Paintings depicting plump pigs, triumphant roosters, and cheerful folk weddings convey heartfelt wishes for prosperity and domestic harmony.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nDong Ho folk woodblock paintings, originating in Bac Ninh (23) ________, are vibrant artistic expressions of traditional Vietnamese rural life. Artisans carve reverse designs onto dense (24) ________ wood blocks, using separate blocks for each distinct colour. Pigments are derived entirely from natural sources: (25) ________ from crushed scallop shells (điệp), black from charred bamboo leaves, red from terra cotta clay, (26) ________ yellow from gardenia seeds. Paintings depicting plump pigs, triumphant roosters, and cheerful folk (27) ________ convey heartfelt wishes for prosperity and domestic harmony.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nDong Ho folk woodblock paintings, originating in Bac Ninh province, are vibrant artistic expressions of traditional Vietnamese rural life. Artisans carve reverse designs onto dense persimmon wood blocks, using separate blocks for each distinct colour. Pigments are derived entirely from natural sources: white from crushed scallop shells (điệp), black from charred bamboo leaves, red from terra cotta clay, and yellow from gardenia seeds. Paintings depicting plump pigs, triumphant roosters, and cheerful folk weddings convey heartfelt wishes for prosperity and domestic harmony.",
