      "audioScript": "Nam: \"Hi Mai! What are you working on for our English group presentation?\"\nMai: \"Hello Nam! I am preparing a short talk about The Role of Youth in Combating Cyberbullying.\"\nNam: \"That sounds very interesting! Can you share one important detail about it?\"\nMai: \"Sure! Cyberbullying on social media networks has emerged as an insidious threat to the emotional safety of secondary school pupils.\"\nNam: \"I agree completely. It helps students understand more about real-life experiences.\"\nMai: \"Yes, and we can practice speaking English with confidence during the presentation!\"",
      "clozeText": "Cyberbullying on social media networks has emerged as an (23) ________ threat to the emotional safety of secondary school pupils. Spreading malicious gossip, posting unconsented photographs, or (24) ________ social exclusion on online messaging groups can drive vulnerable victims into severe despair. Grade 9 (25) ________ must cultivate digital empathy and stand up courageously as active upstanders rather than passive bystanders. Reporting (26) ________ behavior and extending private messages of solidarity to targeted peers can save lives. (27) ________ digital spaces must be anchored in mutual respect.",
      "readingText": "Cyberbullying on social media networks has emerged as an insidious threat to the emotional safety of secondary school pupils. Spreading malicious gossip, posting unconsented photographs, or orchestrating social exclusion on online messaging groups can drive vulnerable victims into severe despair. Grade 9 students must cultivate digital empathy and stand up courageously as active upstanders rather than passive bystanders. Reporting toxic behavior and extending private messages of solidarity to targeted peers can save lives. Our digital spaces must be anchored in mutual respect.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nCyberbullying on social media networks has emerged as an (23) ________ threat to the emotional safety of secondary school pupils. Spreading malicious gossip, posting unconsented photographs, or (24) ________ social exclusion on online messaging groups can drive vulnerable victims into severe despair. Grade 9 (25) ________ must cultivate digital empathy and stand up courageously as active upstanders rather than passive bystanders. Reporting (26) ________ behavior and extending private messages of solidarity to targeted peers can save lives. (27) ________ digital spaces must be anchored in mutual respect.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nCyberbullying on social media networks has emerged as an insidious threat to the emotional safety of secondary school pupils. Spreading malicious gossip, posting unconsented photographs, or orchestrating social exclusion on online messaging groups can drive vulnerable victims into severe despair. Grade 9 students must cultivate digital empathy and stand up courageously as active upstanders rather than passive bystanders. Reporting toxic behavior and extending private messages of solidarity to targeted peers can save lives. Our digital spaces must be anchored in mutual respect.",
