      "audioScript": "Mark: \"Hi Hoa! What are you working on for our English group presentation?\"\nHoa: \"Hello Mark! I am preparing a short talk about The Importance of Balanced Sleep for Teenagers.\"\nMark: \"That sounds very interesting! Can you share one important detail about it?\"\nHoa: \"Sure! Sleep is the biological foundation upon which adolescent neurological development, emotional stability, and academic success depend.\"\nMark: \"I agree completely. It helps students understand more about real-life experiences.\"\nHoa: \"Yes, and we can practice speaking English with confidence during the presentation!\"",
      "clozeText": "Sleep is the biological foundation upon which adolescent neurological (23) ________, emotional stability, and academic success depend. Neuroscientists reveal that during deep REM sleep, the (24) ________ brain consolidates memory traces, prunes redundant neural connections, and flushes out metabolic toxins accumulated (25) ________ waking hours. Unfortunately, intense academic schedules and addictive late-night smartphone scrolling deprive millions of (26) ________ of essential sleep. Establishing a consistent bedtime routine and banning electronic screens (27) ________ hour before sleep ensures restorative cognitive recovery.",
      "readingText": "Sleep is the biological foundation upon which adolescent neurological development, emotional stability, and academic success depend. Neuroscientists reveal that during deep REM sleep, the teenage brain consolidates memory traces, prunes redundant neural connections, and flushes out metabolic toxins accumulated during waking hours. Unfortunately, intense academic schedules and addictive late-night smartphone scrolling deprive millions of teenagers of essential sleep. Establishing a consistent bedtime routine and banning electronic screens one hour before sleep ensures restorative cognitive recovery.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nSleep is the biological foundation upon which adolescent neurological (23) ________, emotional stability, and academic success depend. Neuroscientists reveal that during deep REM sleep, the (24) ________ brain consolidates memory traces, prunes redundant neural connections, and flushes out metabolic toxins accumulated (25) ________ waking hours. Unfortunately, intense academic schedules and addictive late-night smartphone scrolling deprive millions of (26) ________ of essential sleep. Establishing a consistent bedtime routine and banning electronic screens (27) ________ hour before sleep ensures restorative cognitive recovery.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nSleep is the biological foundation upon which adolescent neurological development, emotional stability, and academic success depend. Neuroscientists reveal that during deep REM sleep, the teenage brain consolidates memory traces, prunes redundant neural connections, and flushes out metabolic toxins accumulated during waking hours. Unfortunately, intense academic schedules and addictive late-night smartphone scrolling deprive millions of teenagers of essential sleep. Establishing a consistent bedtime routine and banning electronic screens one hour before sleep ensures restorative cognitive recovery.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Causes of urban heat islands (concrete, asphalt, glass); How trees and pocket parks cool ambient temperatures; Air filtration and psychological benefits.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
