      "audioScript": "David: \"Hi Huong! What are you working on for our English group presentation?\"\nHuong: \"Hello David! I am preparing a short talk about The Concrete Jungle vs. Urban Green Spaces.\"\nDavid: \"That sounds very interesting! Can you share one important detail about it?\"\nHuong: \"Sure! The relentless conversion of urban land into concrete high-rises and asphalt highways has created oppressive 'heat island' effects in metropolitan areas.\"\nDavid: \"I agree completely. It helps students understand more about real-life experiences.\"\nHuong: \"Yes, and we can practice speaking English with confidence during the presentation!\"",
      "clozeText": "The relentless conversion of urban land into concrete high-rises (23) ________ asphalt highways has created oppressive 'heat island' effects in metropolitan areas. Temperatures in concrete downtown (24) ________ can soar up to six degrees higher than surrounding rural outskirts. To restore ecological balance, (25) ________ cities are incorporating rooftop gardens, vertical green walls, and pocket public parks into urban architecture. (26) ________ vegetation purifies toxic air, lowers ambient temperatures, and provides vital psychological refuges for stressed (27) ________. Urban greening is an urgent environmental imperative.",
      "readingText": "The relentless conversion of urban land into concrete high-rises and asphalt highways has created oppressive 'heat island' effects in metropolitan areas. Temperatures in concrete downtown corridors can soar up to six degrees higher than surrounding rural outskirts. To restore ecological balance, progressive cities are incorporating rooftop gardens, vertical green walls, and pocket public parks into urban architecture. Green vegetation purifies toxic air, lowers ambient temperatures, and provides vital psychological refuges for stressed citizens. Urban greening is an urgent environmental imperative.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nThe relentless conversion of urban land into concrete high-rises (23) ________ asphalt highways has created oppressive 'heat island' effects in metropolitan areas. Temperatures in concrete downtown (24) ________ can soar up to six degrees higher than surrounding rural outskirts. To restore ecological balance, (25) ________ cities are incorporating rooftop gardens, vertical green walls, and pocket public parks into urban architecture. (26) ________ vegetation purifies toxic air, lowers ambient temperatures, and provides vital psychological refuges for stressed (27) ________. Urban greening is an urgent environmental imperative.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nThe relentless conversion of urban land into concrete high-rises and asphalt highways has created oppressive 'heat island' effects in metropolitan areas. Temperatures in concrete downtown corridors can soar up to six degrees higher than surrounding rural outskirts. To restore ecological balance, progressive cities are incorporating rooftop gardens, vertical green walls, and pocket public parks into urban architecture. Green vegetation purifies toxic air, lowers ambient temperatures, and provides vital psychological refuges for stressed citizens. Urban greening is an urgent environmental imperative.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): History and location along the Nhue River; Natural silkworm cocoon processing; Distinctive characteristics of vân silk; Adapting silk fashion to modern global markets.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
