      "audioScript": "Phong: \"Hi Lan! What are you working on for our English group presentation?\"\nLan: \"Hello Phong! I am preparing a short talk about Overcoming FOMO and Cultivating Contentment.\"\nPhong: \"That sounds very interesting! Can you share one important detail about it?\"\nLan: \"Sure! The Fear Of Missing Out (FOMO) has become an pervasive emotional dilemma among adolescents immersed in constant digital updates.\"\nPhong: \"I agree completely. It helps students understand more about real-life experiences.\"\nLan: \"Yes, and we can practice speaking English with confidence during the presentation!\"",
      "clozeText": "The Fear Of Missing Out (FOMO) has become an (23) ________ emotional dilemma among adolescents immersed in constant digital updates. Seeing friends post photos of trendy cafe (24) ________ or exclusive parties can trigger intense feelings of isolation and inadequacy. Psychologists encourage teenagers to (25) ________ FOMO with JOMO—the Joy Of Missing Out. JOMO means relishing peaceful quiet moments, immersing oneself in (26) ________ offline passions, and celebrating one's unique life trajectory. Contentment flourishes when we stop (27) ________ our interior lives with other people's curated exteriors.",
      "readingText": "The Fear Of Missing Out (FOMO) has become an pervasive emotional dilemma among adolescents immersed in constant digital updates. Seeing friends post photos of trendy cafe visits or exclusive parties can trigger intense feelings of isolation and inadequacy. Psychologists encourage teenagers to replace FOMO with JOMO—the Joy Of Missing Out. JOMO means relishing peaceful quiet moments, immersing oneself in enriching offline passions, and celebrating one's unique life trajectory. Contentment flourishes when we stop comparing our interior lives with other people's curated exteriors.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nThe Fear Of Missing Out (FOMO) has become an (23) ________ emotional dilemma among adolescents immersed in constant digital updates. Seeing friends post photos of trendy cafe (24) ________ or exclusive parties can trigger intense feelings of isolation and inadequacy. Psychologists encourage teenagers to (25) ________ FOMO with JOMO—the Joy Of Missing Out. JOMO means relishing peaceful quiet moments, immersing oneself in (26) ________ offline passions, and celebrating one's unique life trajectory. Contentment flourishes when we stop (27) ________ our interior lives with other people's curated exteriors.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nThe Fear Of Missing Out (FOMO) has become an pervasive emotional dilemma among adolescents immersed in constant digital updates. Seeing friends post photos of trendy cafe visits or exclusive parties can trigger intense feelings of isolation and inadequacy. Psychologists encourage teenagers to replace FOMO with JOMO—the Joy Of Missing Out. JOMO means relishing peaceful quiet moments, immersing oneself in enriching offline passions, and celebrating one's unique life trajectory. Contentment flourishes when we stop comparing our interior lives with other people's curated exteriors.",
      "writingRubric": "Tiêu chí chấm điểm (1.0đ): Neurobiological effects of aerobic exertion (BDNF, endorphins); Releasing accumulated study tension; Memory and concentration benefits; Recommended routines.",
      "sampleWritingText": "In my opinion, engaging in productive activities during free time plays a crucial role in teenagers' overall development. First, it provides a healthy balance between rigorous academic studies and physical recreation, helping students alleviate stress. Furthermore, participating in school clubs or community projects broadens practical knowledge and strengthens social bonding. Therefore, choosing meaningful hobbies is essential for a joyful and well-rounded teenage life.",
