      "audioScript": "Tom: \"Hi Linh! What are you working on for our English group presentation?\"\nLinh: \"Hello Tom! I am preparing a short talk about Preserving Tranh Khuc Banh Chung Village Heritage.\"\nTom: \"That sounds very interesting! Can you share one important detail about it?\"\nLinh: \"Sure! Tranh Khuc village in Thanh Tri district is celebrated throughout Vietnam as the premier guild village for wrapping traditional Square Sticky Rice Cakes (bánh chưng).\"\nTom: \"I agree completely. It helps students understand more about real-life experiences.\"\nLinh: \"Yes, and we can practice speaking English with confidence during the presentation!\"",
      "clozeText": "Tranh Khuc village in Thanh Tri district is celebrated throughout (23) ________ as the premier guild village for wrapping traditional Square Sticky Rice Cakes (bánh chưng). During the (24) ________ preceding the Lunar New Year, the entire village hums with bustling activity. Artisans skillfully wash green (25) ________ leaves, soak white fragrant glutinous rice, and prepare seasoned pork belly and golden mung beans. Wrapped (26) ________ mathematical precision into square bamboo molds and boiled over wood fires for twelve hours, Tranh (27) ________ cakes embody deep ancestral gratitude and national identity.",
      "readingText": "Tranh Khuc village in Thanh Tri district is celebrated throughout Vietnam as the premier guild village for wrapping traditional Square Sticky Rice Cakes (bánh chưng). During the weeks preceding the Lunar New Year, the entire village hums with bustling activity. Artisans skillfully wash green dong leaves, soak white fragrant glutinous rice, and prepare seasoned pork belly and golden mung beans. Wrapped with mathematical precision into square bamboo molds and boiled over wood fires for twelve hours, Tranh Khuc cakes embody deep ancestral gratitude and national identity.",
      "passageText": "📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐIỀN TỪ (CLOZE TEXT):\nTranh Khuc village in Thanh Tri district is celebrated throughout (23) ________ as the premier guild village for wrapping traditional Square Sticky Rice Cakes (bánh chưng). During the (24) ________ preceding the Lunar New Year, the entire village hums with bustling activity. Artisans skillfully wash green (25) ________ leaves, soak white fragrant glutinous rice, and prepare seasoned pork belly and golden mung beans. Wrapped (26) ________ mathematical precision into square bamboo molds and boiled over wood fires for twelve hours, Tranh (27) ________ cakes embody deep ancestral gratitude and national identity.\n\n📖 ĐOẠN VĂN ĐỌC HIỂU (READING PASSAGE):\nTranh Khuc village in Thanh Tri district is celebrated throughout Vietnam as the premier guild village for wrapping traditional Square Sticky Rice Cakes (bánh chưng). During the weeks preceding the Lunar New Year, the entire village hums with bustling activity. Artisans skillfully wash green dong leaves, soak white fragrant glutinous rice, and prepare seasoned pork belly and golden mung beans. Wrapped with mathematical precision into square bamboo molds and boiled over wood fires for twelve hours, Tranh Khuc cakes embody deep ancestral gratitude and national identity.",
